WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.907
"Is Obesity Caused by a GLP-1
Hormone Deficiency?"

00:00:06.907 --> 00:00:10.811
Can we drug our way
out of the obesity crisis?

00:00:10.811 --> 00:00:12.412
This 60 Minutes episode

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.414
certainly seemed to suggest
we could.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:15.649
Only later did we learn

00:00:15.649 --> 00:00:18.652
that 60 Minutes had been paid
by the makers of Ozempic

00:00:18.652 --> 00:00:21.054
to air a 13-minute
promotional segment

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:24.658
and pass it off
as a news story.

00:00:24.658 --> 00:00:27.794
Are these GLP-1 drugs the answer
to the obesity epidemic?

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.096
The head of
the European Association

00:00:29.096 --> 00:00:31.899
for the Study of Obesity
was pretty bullish,

00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:34.768
conveniently failing to disclose
that his group had received

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:38.238
millions of dollars
from the drug maker.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:41.375
But doesn’t getting
a tiny weekly injection

00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:44.411
sound far easier than getting
all sweaty in the gym?

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.713
Do these game-changing
new medications

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:50.684
"make lifestyle-based treatment
of obesity obsolete"?

00:00:50.684 --> 00:00:54.554
Let’s ask those paid by
the two main GLP-1 drug makers,

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.256
which now have
a combined net worth

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:59.660
greater than a trillion dollars.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.828
The World Obesity Federation,

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.563
which evidently just got
a million dollars

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.098
from the Ozempic company,

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.501
published a consensus statement
in one of its journals

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:11.705
favoring the definition
of obesity as a disease.

00:01:11.705 --> 00:01:14.141
This designation
may not benefit patients,

00:01:14.141 --> 00:01:16.243
but it will benefit doctors
and drug companies

00:01:16.243 --> 00:01:17.978
when health insurance
and clinical guidelines

00:01:17.978 --> 00:01:20.547
promote treatment
with drugs and surgery.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:23.817
A concern is that labeling
obesity as a disease

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.652
risks reducing our autonomy,

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:28.221
disempowering and robbing us
of the intrinsic motivation

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.324
that’s an important enabler
of change.

00:01:30.324 --> 00:01:31.959
It encourages fatalism,

00:01:31.959 --> 00:01:35.562
promoting the fallacy
that genetics are destiny.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:38.632
But, of course,
it can’t be our genes.

00:01:38.632 --> 00:01:41.368
The obesity epidemic only
started a few decades ago.

00:01:41.368 --> 00:01:43.603
Our genes didn’t somehow
magically change

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.639
in the late 1970s.

00:01:45.639 --> 00:01:48.175
Others blame lack of willpower,

00:01:48.175 --> 00:01:50.143
but that doesn’t make
any sense either.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:53.780
All of us coincidentally lost
our collective self-control?

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.484
It’s the food.

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.152
The rise in the number
of excess calories

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.654
provided by the U.S. food supply

00:02:00.654 --> 00:02:04.524
is more than sufficient
to explain the obesity epidemic.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:07.561
Obesity is not
some moral failing.

00:02:07.561 --> 00:02:11.231
The battle of the bulge is
a battle against biology.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:13.367
We’re living
in a toxic food environment,

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.235
drowning in a sea
of excess calories,

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:19.139
being bombarded with ads
for fast food and candy.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:22.709
Becoming overweight is
a normal, natural response

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:26.046
to the abnormal,
unnatural ubiquity

00:02:26.046 --> 00:02:29.216
of sugary, fatty foods that are
concentrated with calories.

00:02:29.216 --> 00:02:31.618
So, the prime cause
for the obesity epidemic

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:34.054
is neither gluttony nor sloth.

00:02:34.054 --> 00:02:35.722
Being overweight may simply be

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.724
a normal response,
by normal people,

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.793
to an abnormal situation.

00:02:39.793 --> 00:02:42.429
And with nearly three-quarters
of Americans overweight,

00:02:42.429 --> 00:02:44.765
it’s literally normal.

00:02:44.765 --> 00:02:47.367
So, if obesity is
to be understood

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:51.204
as "normal physiology within
a pathological environment,"

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.607
there is an argument
that drugs like Ozempic

00:02:53.607 --> 00:02:57.144
really aren’t tackling
the root cause of obesity.

00:02:57.144 --> 00:02:59.813
These drugs will likely have
only a modest effect

00:02:59.813 --> 00:03:01.915
on reducing
the rapidly growing epidemic

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:04.418
and may even make it worse,

00:03:04.418 --> 00:03:05.986
as Big Pharma and its lobbyists

00:03:05.986 --> 00:03:08.822
try to shift society’s focus
to drugs

00:03:08.822 --> 00:03:11.758
rather than broader
public health strategies.

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:15.028
The real solution would involve
fixing the food system,

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.197
but why would Big Food
change its ways

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:19.466
if obesity can be treated
with drugs?

00:03:19.466 --> 00:03:23.070
So, the main actors responsible
for creating and perpetuating

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:27.707
the obesity-generating world
will continue undisturbed.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:30.811
England’s health secretary
was keen to use GLP-1 drugs

00:03:30.811 --> 00:03:32.679
as a "way of preventing illness

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:35.749
without resorting
to ’nanny state’ measures,"

00:03:35.749 --> 00:03:37.951
but advocates are just
talking about things like

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:41.655
restricting the thousands of ads
kids see every year

00:03:41.655 --> 00:03:44.858
for candy, liquid candy
(soft drinks),

00:03:44.858 --> 00:03:48.161
breakfast candy, and fast food.

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.696
A quarter century ago,

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:53.400
the term "Social Determinants
of Health" was coined,

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.436
defined as the nonmedical
factors that influence health

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.939
too often ignored
by the medical establishment,

00:03:58.939 --> 00:04:00.307
such as poverty.

00:04:00.307 --> 00:04:02.742
They explain why the top
1 percent, for example,

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:07.514
live about 10 to 15 years longer
than the bottom 1 percent.

00:04:07.514 --> 00:04:09.449
More recently,
based on experience

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.251
with the alcohol
and tobacco industries,

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.753
the concept of "Commercial
Determinants of Health"

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:14.821
was introduced,

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.724
which can be defined as
"factors that influence health

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:20.861
which stem from the profit
motive," also referred to

00:04:20.861 --> 00:04:23.430
as the Corporate
Determinants of Health.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.699
The food and beverage sectors
spend huge amounts

00:04:25.699 --> 00:04:27.801
on developing
and marketing products

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:29.402
packed with sugar,
fat, and salt,

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:32.239
deliberately designed
to lead to addictive consumption

00:04:32.239 --> 00:04:34.207
that contributes
to the increasing prevalence

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.676
of chronic disease.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:39.913
Public corporations like
Coca-Cola have a legal duty

00:04:39.913 --> 00:04:43.016
to maximize return
to their shareholders,

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.217
and those running the companies

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:46.953
are heavily incentivized
to achieve this.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:49.055
Many observers are outraged
by stories

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:51.958
of what some of these companies
do to maximize returns,

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:55.795
but as people working in the
tobacco industry can testify,

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:59.132
being the subject
of widespread disrepute

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:03.570
is more than offset
by the financial rewards.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.972
And psychological defense
mechanisms can take care

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.975
of any residual unease about
contributing to the suffering

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:12.746
and death of fellow humans whom
they do not personally know.

00:05:12.746 --> 00:05:15.549
The greatest challenge
to improving health may lie

00:05:15.549 --> 00:05:16.683
in the tension between

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:19.920
wealth creation
and health creation.

